From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/videoout: PC5's 120 Hz setting declares the
 high-frame-rate output

With 120 Hz output on, the display stayed at 59.94 Hz in every game
(Batman: Arkham Origins on a TV that takes 120 Hz: PW_WINE64 found the
output supported, Wine offered the game 3840x2160@120, and RADV logged
nothing about 119.88 Hz). RADV asks for 119.88 Hz only where
/app0/sce_sys/param.json declares it, and a game's process can't open
that file: once /data is granted, the process sees the console's real
root, where /app0 doesn't exist (prospero-win's wine64_main uses the
sandbox's view of app0 for the same reason). The check failed silently.

PW_PC5_HIGH_REFRESH=1, PC5's setting turned on, now declares it: PC5's
own param.json does. Without the variable param.json still decides, and
the log now says when 120 Hz output wasn't asked for.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
index a56559d..42f9b80 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
@@ -369,6 +369,11 @@ videoout_title_declares_high_frame_rate(void)
    const char *const wanted = getenv("PW_PC5_HIGH_REFRESH");
    if (wanted && !strcmp(wanted, "0"))
       return false;
+   /* PW_PC5_HIGH_REFRESH=1: PC5's setting is on, and PC5's param.json declares
+    * the output. A game's process can't read it: once /data is granted, the
+    * process sees the console's real root, where /app0 doesn't exist. */
+   if (wanted && !strcmp(wanted, "1"))
+      return true;
    FILE *const file = fopen("/app0/sce_sys/param.json", "rb");
    if (file == NULL)
       return false;
@@ -446,6 +451,8 @@ videoout_open_locked(void)
          fprintf(stderr, "wsi/videoout: 119.88 Hz %s (%d); presenting at 59.94 Hz\n",
                  supported > 0 ? "refused" : "not supported", configured);
       }
+   } else {
+      fprintf(stderr, "wsi/videoout: 120 Hz output not asked for; presenting at 59.94 Hz\n");
    }
    return true;
 }
